WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 2.2 · Theory of Change
Defining the problem

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Understand why the problem persists before you settle on your solution.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:24.430
Defining the problem means describing the current situation, who experiences it and what keeps it in place, kept separate from the solution you have in mind.

4
00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:25.430
A problem tree in three parts

5
00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:35.278
Trunk: core problem: What is the problem, for whom and where? For example: Young people in our neighbourhood who left school early cannot find a first job.

6
00:00:35.278 --> 00:00:44.756
Roots: causes: Why does this happen? Ask again for each answer. For example: No qualifications, no work experience, few contacts, low confidence and employers’ doubts.

7
00:00:44.756 --> 00:00:54.693
Branches: consequences: What happens because of it? For example: Long spells without work, low income and young people losing hope of local jobs.

8
00:00:55.093 --> 00:00:55.693
Why it matters

9
00:00:55.693 --> 00:01:00.626
1. It checks whether your idea addresses a real cause.

10
00:01:00.626 --> 00:01:05.559
2. It stops you starting from a solution you love.

11
00:01:05.559 --> 00:01:11.863
3. It shows which causes a small, new initiative can influence.

12
00:01:12.263 --> 00:01:12.863
What it guides

13
00:01:12.863 --> 00:01:17.796
1. Your outcomes: changes that tackle the causes you chose.

14
00:01:17.796 --> 00:01:22.359
2. Your assumptions: uncertain causes become hypotheses to test.

15
00:01:22.359 --> 00:01:29.774
3. Your scope: what you will and will not take on at the start.

16
00:01:30.174 --> 00:01:30.774
What to avoid

17
00:01:30.774 --> 00:01:36.448
Naming the missing solution (“no service like ours”) as the problem.

18
00:01:36.448 --> 00:01:41.752
Building the tree for the people affected, not with them.

19
00:01:41.752 --> 00:01:48.056
Collecting personal stories or sensitive data without reason and safeguards.

20
00:01:48.656 --> 00:01:50.456
You write the problem, its scope, causes and one question to investigate.

21
00:01:50.456 --> 00:01:54.456
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:01:55.956 --> 00:01:59.056
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
